.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_HOLD_DRIVER 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_hold_driver ,
.Nm ndi_rele_driver
.Nd hold and release the driver bound to a device
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "struct dev_ops *"
.Fo ndi_hold_driver
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fc
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_rele_driver
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va dip
Device node bound to the driver being held or released.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
\fBndi_hold_driver()\fP obtains a module reference to the driver bound to \fBdip\fP,
loading it if necessary, and returns its device operations vector.
It does not bind an unbound node or attach a device instance.
The node must be at least in the bound state.
.Pp
After a successful hold, call \fBndi_rele_driver()\fP with the same node to release
the driver reference.
The caller must keep the node and its driver binding valid across both calls.
Do not release a failed hold or use the returned operations vector after the
last module reference is released.
.Sh CONTEXT
These functions may be called from user or kernel context.
They may sleep.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
\fBndi_hold_driver()\fP returns a pointer to \fBstruct dev_ops\fP, or \fBNULL\fP
if the node is unbound or the driver cannot be held.
\fBndi_rele_driver()\fP has no return value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_devi_online 9F ,
.Xr ndi_hold_devi 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F ,
.Xr dev_ops 9S
